.Sh ENVIRONMENT
Options override the environment, which overrides the configuration file.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev CREATURE_BODY_CONFIG
Configuration file, when
.Fl -config
is not given.
.It Ev CREATURE_SERVER_HOST , Ev CREATURE_SERVER_PORT , Ev CREATURE_SERVER_TLS
The Creature Server whose sensor reports are followed.
.It Ev CREATURE_PROXY_HOST , Ev CREATURE_PROXY_API_KEY
Reach the server through the proxy instead.
.It Ev CREATURE_WORLD_URL
Creature World API root.
.It Ev OTEL_*
OpenTelemetry export (OTEL_SERVICE_NAME, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS,
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL).
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/creature/body.json
Configuration: server and World addresses, reporting intervals, sensor thresholds and the
characters to follow. A conffile; upgrades
keep local edits.
.It Pa /etc/default/creature-body
Environment overrides for the service, mode 0600. A proxy API key lives here and nowhere else.
.It Pa /usr/lib/systemd/system/creature-body.service
The unit. It runs as a
.Li DynamicUser
and is not started on install:
.Dl systemctl enable --now creature-body
.It Pa /usr/share/doc/creature-body/creature-body-manual.md
The operator's manual, including every configuration key.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl creature-body --server-host 127.0.0.1 --server-port 8000 --log-level debug
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr creature-world 8 ,
.Xr creature-house 8
